<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34643" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕr-argūtus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Very shrill</i> (Appuleian): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tintinnabula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 10, p. 247, 39</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">carmen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Flor. p. 349</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Very acute</i>, <i>very witty</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">homo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Brut. 45, 167</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
